description:
Build a hash table from strings to ints with separate chaining. The types and the hash function are given; write the rest in `solution.c`:

```c
struct entry { char *key; int value; struct entry *next; };
struct table { struct entry **buckets; size_t bucket_count; size_t size; };

bool table_init(struct table *t, size_t bucket_count);   /* all buckets empty (calloc) */
bool table_put(struct table *t, const char *key, int value);
        /* updates the value if the key exists, otherwise adds an entry with its OWN copy of the key.
           After adding, if size > bucket_count, grow to twice as many buckets. */
bool table_get(const struct table *t, const char *key, int *value);   /* false if absent */
bool table_remove(struct table *t, const char *key);
void table_free(struct table *t);                          /* frees everything; the table becomes empty */
```

A key goes in bucket `hash(key) % bucket_count`. Growing means allocating the new bucket array and moving every existing entry (no copying of keys) into its new bucket.

